Functions in C instead, and slow ones
-------------------------------------

memcmp comes from libterae's own C, in src/port/generic, which
port_memcmp.c in this folder includes. Nothing in it is taken from
elsewhere. Why there is no assembly for it:

memcmp   No permissively licensed scalar assembly memcmp exists for RISC-V.
         newlib's memcmp-asm.S needs the vector extension and carries no
         copyright or licence notice.

memcpy and memmove are provided, but only as loops that copy one byte at a
time. FreeBSD's faster memcpy.S and memset.S, which src/port/riscv64 uses,
are written for 64-bit registers only. Android's are 64-bit and need the
vector extension. musl has no RISC-V assembly for these functions.


